    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup tonight is anchored by **Bryce Harper**, who stands as our clear-cut elite play with an 80.21 score against Scherzer. His projection is bolstered by an elite 19% boost from the opposing starter's high xERA and an impressive 33-PA BvP history that adds significant upside. Complementing him are **Justin Crawford** (69.88), **Luis Arraez** (69.53), and **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02). **Justin Crawford** benefits immensely from the matchup against Scherzer, while **Jung Hoo Lee** gains a massive 18% lift from hitting in the two-hole against Jobe. We are leaning heavily into the platoon advantages tonight, particularly with **JJ Bleday**, whose 62.21 score is heavily predicated on a +14% dynamic platoon boost against Alvarez, and **Brendan Donovan**, who similarly earns a +14% edge against Legumina.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Gavin Sheets**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 50.45 score. While his platoon matchup against Lambert is favorable, he ultimately fell behind the likes of **Cal Raleigh** and **Tyler Freeman** due to a lower overall efficiency ceiling and a negative park factor. We remain cautious with **Lawrence Butler**; despite his raw talent, his 51.40 score is suppressed by a significant -13% platoon penalty against Bennett, making him a fringe start. While we aren't facing a true ace tonight, we are wary of **Daulton Varsho**\u2019s matchup against King, M, whose 46% success rate in holding runners effectively neutralizes the stolen base potential we usually demand for a full green light. Keep an eye on **Cal Raleigh**, who sits at the lower end of our active tier; his spot in the 8-hole is a drag on his output, and he will need to capitalize early against Legumina to justify his spot over players like **Masyn Winn** or **Gleyber Torres**.",
